and slash commands both check your staff\nand admin roles (or **Manage Channels**)."},"597":{"id":"/docs/faq","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"page","content":"FAQ","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq"},"598":{"id":"/docs/faq-0","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Short answers to the questions people ask most."},"599":{"id":"/docs/faq-1","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-to-keep-the-bot-online-or-host-anything","content":"Do I need to keep the bot online or host anything?"},"600":{"id":"/docs/faq-2","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-any-privileged-intents","content":"Do I need any privileged intents?"},"601":{"id":"/docs/faq-3","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#how-much-does-it-cost","content":"How much does it cost?"},"602":{"id":"/docs/faq-4","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-have-more-than-one-panel","content":"Can I have more than one panel?"},"603":{"id":"/docs/faq-5","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#channels-or-threads","content":"Channels or threads?"},"604":{"id":"/docs/faq-6","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#how-many-ticket-types-per-panel","content":"How many ticket types per panel?"},"605":{"id":"/docs/faq-7","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-users-see-each-others-tickets","content":"Can users see each other's tickets?"},"606":{"id":"/docs/faq-8","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#are-internal-notes-visible-to-the-user","content":"Are internal notes visible to the user?"},"607":{"id":"/docs/faq-9","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#where-are-transcripts-stored","content":"Where are transcripts stored?"},"608":{"id":"/docs/faq-10","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-block-someone-from-opening-tickets","content":"Can I block someone from opening tickets?"},"609":{"id":"/docs/faq-11","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-wording-and-colours","content":"Can I change the wording and colours?"},"610":{"id":"/docs/faq-12","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-bots-name-and-avatar-in-my-server","content":"Can I change the bot's name and avatar in my server?"},"611":{"id":"/docs/faq-13","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#are-there-ready-made-panel-templates","content":"Are there ready-made panel templates?"},"612":{"id":"/docs/faq-14","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#how-do-i-sign-out-of-the-dashboard","content":"How do I sign out of the dashboard?"},"613":{"id":"/docs/faq-15","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#why-cant-my-staff-see-thread-tickets","content":"Why can't my staff see thread tickets?"},"614":{"id":"/docs/faq-16","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#is-there-a-list-of-all-limits","content":"Is there a list of all limits?"},"615":{"id":"/docs/faq-17","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#where-are-the-terms-and-privacy-policy","content":"Where are the Terms and Privacy Policy?"},"616":{"id":"/docs/faq-18","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#does-it-support-other-languages","content":"Does it support other languages?"},"617":{"id":"/docs/faq-19","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#is-it-open-source-can-i-self-host-it","content":"Is it open source? Can I self-host it?"},"618":{"id":"/docs/faq-20","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-to-keep-the-bot-online-or-host-anything","content":"No. dat one ticketer is a hosted service. There's nothing for you to run or keep alive - you just\ninvite the bot and it works."},"619":{"id":"/docs/faq-21","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#do-i-need-any-privileged-intents","content":"No. It only reacts to the buttons, commands and menus it posts; it never reads ordinary chat\nmessages."},"620":{"id":"/docs/faq-22","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#how-much-does-it-cost","content":"Nothing to you - just invite the bot and use it."},"621":{"id":"/docs/faq-23","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-have-more-than-one-panel","content":"Yes - as many as you like, in different channels, each with its own types, style, channels and\noverrides. Use **Duplicate** to copy one."},"622":{"id":"/docs/faq-24","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#channels-or-threads","content":"Both. Set it server-wide and override per panel (or per nothing - channels and threads are a\npanel-level choice). Threads are private, auto-archive after 7 days, and are archived + locked on\nclose instead of deleted."},"623":{"id":"/docs/faq-25","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#how-many-ticket-types-per-panel","content":"25 with **Dropdown**, 5 with **Buttons** (Discord's row limit)."},"624":{"id":"/docs/faq-26","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-users-see-each-others-tickets","content":"No. Tickets are private - only the opener, staff/admin roles and anyone explicitly added can see\nthem."},"625":{"id":"/docs/faq-27","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#are-internal-notes-visible-to-the-user","content":"No. Notes are stored on the ticket, posted to the log channel, and never shown to the opener or\nincluded in transcripts."},"626":{"id":"/docs/faq-28","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#where-are-transcripts-stored","content":"They're kept by the service (so they show up in the **Transcripts** tab) and posted to your\ntranscript or log channel as an HTML file. The opener can also get a DM copy."},"627":{"id":"/docs/faq-29","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-block-someone-from-opening-tickets","content":"Yes - use the **Ticket blacklist** (dashboard) or `/blacklist add`."},"628":{"id":"/docs/faq-30","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-wording-and-colours","content":"Yes, extensively - server-wide, per panel and (for some fields) per ticket type. See\nCustomization."},"629":{"id":"/docs/faq-31","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#can-i-change-the-bots-name-and-avatar-in-my-server","content":"Yes. The **Bot profile (this server)** card sets a nickname, avatar, banner and bio for your server\nonly. See Server profile."},"630":{"id":"/docs/faq-32","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#are-there-ready-made-panel-templates","content":"Yes - `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` and `Ban appeal`, plus `Blank`. See\nPanel templates."},"631":{"id":"/docs/faq-33","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#how-do-i-sign-out-of-the-dashboard","content":"Use the **Sign out** link in the header, or open `/oauth/logout` - either clears your session."},"632":{"id":"/docs/faq-34","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#why-cant-my-staff-see-thread-tickets","content":"Private threads only show up for their members and users with **Manage Threads**. The bot adds the\nopener but not your staff roles. Grant **Manage Threads**, **Add User** the staff member, or use\nchannel tickets instead. See How a ticket opens."},"633":{"id":"/docs/faq-35","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#is-there-a-list-of-all-limits","content":"Yes - Limits & quotas covers panels, types, ticket fields and dashboard\nlists."},"634":{"id":"/docs/faq-36","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#where-are-the-terms-and-privacy-policy","content":"Both are linked in the dashboard header and footer: `/terms.html` and `/privacy.html`. They are\nsummarised on Terms & privacy."},"635":{"id":"/docs/faq-37","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#does-it-support-other-languages","content":"The UI text can be preset to English, Spanish, French, German or Portuguese, and every message is\neditable, so you can write it in any language."},"636":{"id":"/docs/faq-38","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#is-it-open-source-can-i-self-host-it","content":"No. dat one ticketer is closed source and only runs as the hosted service - you use it by inviting\nthe bot to your server."},"637":{"id":"/docs/getting-started","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting started","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started"},"638":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"Invite the bot, sign in, and open your first ticket."},"639":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"1. Invite the bot to your server"},"640":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"2. Sign in to the dashboard"},"641":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"3. Do the one-minute config"},"642":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"4. Create your first panel"},"643":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"5. Test it"},"644":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"Where to next"},"645":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"This is the fast path. Ten minutes end to end."},"646":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"Open the dashboard at\n`dat-one-ticketer.danhost.workers.dev`."},"647":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"Click **Invite the bot** (or **Add to Server**). This opens Discord's authorise screen."},"648":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#1-invite-the-bot-to-your-server","content":"Pick your server and approve. The bot needs the permissions it lists - see\nPermissions if you want to know why."},"649":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"On the landing page click **Sign in with Discord**."},"650":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"Authorise the app."},"651":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"You land on **Servers** (`#/`). You see every server where you are the **owner** or have\n**Manage Server** - others are hidden."},"652":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#2-sign-in-to-the-dashboard","content":"To sign out later, use the **Sign out** link in the header, or open `/oauth/logout` directly."},"653":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"You can do all of this from the dashboard, or from Discord with slash commands."},"654":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Open your server in the dashboard and, in **General settings**:"},"655":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Default ticket mode** - `Private channel` or `Private thread`."},"656":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Default category** - where new channel tickets go."},"657":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Staff roles** - who is allowed to claim and manage tickets."},"658":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Set **Log channel** and **Transcript channel** (optional but recommended)."},"659":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"Click **Save settings**."},"660":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#3-do-the-one-minute-config","content":"If the server page shows **\"Add the bot to continue\"**, click **Add to Server** before anything\nelse - nothing works until the bot is actually in the server."},"661":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"On the server page, in the **Ticket panels** card, click **+ New panel**."},"662":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-24","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Pick a template in **Start from a template** - `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` or\n`Ban appeal` - or leave it on `Blank`."},"663":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-25","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Set **Channel to post in** and the **Title** / **Description** users will see."},"664":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-26","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Add at least one **Ticket type** (a label like `General Support`)."},"665":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-27","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"Click **Create panel**."},"666":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-28","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#4-create-your-first-panel","content":"The panel message is posted to the channel you chose. Users can now click it to open a ticket."},"667":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-29","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Open Discord, go to the panel channel, and click the panel as if you were a user. You should get a\nprivate channel/thread with a welcome message and a row of buttons."},"668":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-30","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Then:"},"669":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-31","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Click **Claim** to take the ticket."},"670":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-32","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#5-test-it","content":"Click **Close** to close it - a transcript is generated and sent to your transcript (or log)\nchannel."},"671":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-33","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Launch checklist\" href=\"/docs/checklist\" />"},"672":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-34","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Setup recipes\" href=\"/docs/recipes\" />"},"673":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-35","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Tour the dashboard\" href=\"/docs/dashboard\" />"},"674":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-36","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Full settings reference\" href=\"/docs/dashboard/settings\" />"},"675":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-37","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Slash commands\" href=\"/docs/discord/commands\" />"},"676":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-38","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#where-to-next","content":"<Card title=\"Placeholders\" href=\"/docs/customization/placeholders\" />"},"677":{"id":"/docs/glossary","page_id":"/docs/glossary","type":"page","content":"Glossary","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/glossary"},"678":{"id":"/docs/glossary-0","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"The words dat one ticketer uses, and what they mean."},"679":{"id":"/docs/glossary-1","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Admin role**\n: A higher-tier staff role. Admins additionally get **Manage Channels** inside channel tickets."},"680":{"id":"/docs/glossary-2","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Audit log**\n: A reverse-chronological record of settings, panel, blacklist and ticket changes, each with an\nactor ID and timestamp."},"681":{"id":"/docs/glossary-3","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Blacklist**\n: A list of users who cannot open tickets in a server."},"682":{"id":"/docs/glossary-4","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Bot profile**\n: The nickname, avatar, banner and bio the bot shows in one server, set on the server page. It does\nnot change the bot globally."},"683":{"id":"/docs/glossary-5","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Button panel**\n: A panel that shows one button per ticket type (max 5)."},"684":{"id":"/docs/glossary-6","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Channel ticket**\n: A private channel created for a single ticket."},"685":{"id":"/docs/glossary-7","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Claim**\n: A staff member marking themselves as handling a ticket."},"686":{"id":"/docs/glossary-8","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Customization**\n: The messages, colours, buttons and priorities that shape how tickets look and read. Set\nserver-wide, per panel, and per type."},"687":{"id":"/docs/glossary-9","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Dropdown panel**\n: A panel that shows a select menu of ticket types (max 25)."},"688":{"id":"/docs/glossary-10","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Internal note**\n: A staff-only note on a ticket. Never shown to the opener and never included in transcripts."},"689":{"id":"/docs/glossary-11","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Log channel**\n: The channel that receives ticket activity and internal notes. Also used for transcripts when no\ntranscript channel is set."},"690":{"id":"/docs/glossary-12","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Max open tickets**\n: The per-user cap on open tickets. Staff bypass it, and a ticket type can add its own cap."},"691":{"id":"/docs/glossary-13","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Panel**\n: A message in a channel with a dropdown or buttons that opens tickets."},"692":{"id":"/docs/glossary-14","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Panel template**\n: A starting point in the new-panel editor - `Blank`, `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` or\n`Ban appeal`. It fills in the panel message and ticket types; everything stays editable."},"693":{"id":"/docs/glossary-15","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Placeholder**\n: A `{token}` in a text field that is replaced with a real value, e.g. `{username}`."},"694":{"id":"/docs/glossary-16","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Priority**\n: Low / Normal / High / Urgent (or your own list). Used by the Priority button and shown on the\nwelcome embed."},"695":{"id":"/docs/glossary-17","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Private thread**\n: A thread only visible to its members and users with **Manage Threads**. Used for thread tickets."},"696":{"id":"/docs/glossary-18","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Staff**\n: Anyone with **Manage Channels**, or any role listed in Staff roles or Admin roles."},"697":{"id":"/docs/glossary-19","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Sub-type**\n: A second choice under a ticket type, e.g. `Bug report → Crash`."},"698":{"id":"/docs/glossary-20","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Tag**\n: A short free-text label staff can put on a ticket."},"699":{"id":"/docs/glossary-21","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Ticket**\n: A single support conversation, opened from a panel and living in its own channel or thread."},"700":{"id":"/docs/glossary-22","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Ticket type**\n: One option on a panel, e.g. `General Support` or `Sales`."},"701":{"id":"/docs/glossary-23","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Transcript**\n: A styled HTML copy of a ticket's messages, generated when the ticket closes."},"702":{"id":"/docs/glossary-24","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Transcript channel**\n: The channel where closed-ticket transcripts are posted. Falls back to the log channel, and the\ntranscript is always saved even if neither is set."},"703":{"id":"/docs/glossary-25","page_id":"/docs/glossary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/glossary","content":"**Thread ticket**\n: A private thread created for a single ticket (auto-archives after 7 days; archived + locked on\nclose)."},"704":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"705":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"What dat one ticketer is, where you use it, and what it can do."},"706":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"The two places you use it"},"707":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"What it can do"},"708":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#who-this-wiki-is-for","content":"Who this wiki is for"},"709":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**dat one ticketer** is a Discord ticketing bot. Users click a panel in your server, a private\nchannel or thread opens for them, and your staff manage it with buttons or slash commands. Every\nticket can be exported as an HTML transcript when it closes."},"710":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"It's a hosted service - you just invite the bot. There's nothing to install and nothing to keep\nonline, and a dashboard where you set everything up and read your ticket history."},"711":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"| Place                 | What for                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **The web dashboard** | Set everything up: panels, ticket types, messages, colours, channels, staff roles, blacklists, transcripts, stats and the audit log. |","table":"table-0"},"712":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"| Place       | What for                                                                                       |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Discord** | Where users open tickets from a panel and staff claim, rename, tag, prioritise and close them. |","table":"table-0"},"713":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"You sign in to the dashboard **with Discord**. In Discord itself you only need the bot in your\nserver - use the **Add to Server** / **Invite the bot** button."},"714":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-two-places-you-use-it","content":"The dashboard lives at\n`dat-one-ticketer.danhost.workers.dev`."},"715":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"A message with a dropdown or buttons. Each option is a ticket type (\"Bug report\",\n\"Ban appeal\", ...). Post as many panels as you like."},"716":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Each ticket opens either as a private channel or a private thread, server-wide or per panel or\nper type."},"717":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"When a ticket closes, a styled HTML copy of every message is saved, posted to a channel, and\noptionally DMed to the opener."},"718":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Welcome embeds, button labels/emoji/styles, custom priorities, all system messages and the\ntranscript embed - with `{placeholders}`."},"719":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Claim, add/remove users, rename, tags, internal notes (never shown to the user) and priorities."},"720":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"A nickname, avatar, banner and bio for the bot in your server alone."},"721":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Complete configurations for support, reports, sales and ban appeals."},"722":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"The short list to run through before you announce your panel."},"723":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-it-can-do","content":"Totals, open counts, per-staff claimed/closed counts, and a reverse-chronological log of every\nchange."},"724":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#who-this-wiki-is-for","content":"**Server owners & admins** who want to invite the bot and configure it - start with\nGetting started."},"725":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#who-this-wiki-is-for","content":"**Staff** who live in tickets - read Using tickets."},"726":{"id":"/docs-21","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#who-this-wiki-is-for","content":"**Anyone curious about the settings** - the Dashboard and\nCustomization sections cover every field and button."},"727":{"id":"/docs/legal","page_id":"/docs/legal","type":"page","content":"Terms & privacy","breadcrumbs":["dat one ticketer"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/legal"},"728":{"id":"/docs/legal-0","page_id":"/docs/legal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/legal","content":"Where the legal pages live and what they cover."},"729":{"id":"/docs/legal-1","page_id":"/docs/legal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/legal#terms-of-service---in-short","content":"Terms of Service - in short"},"730":{"id":"/docs/legal-2","page_id":"/docs/legal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/legal#privacy-policy---in-short","content":"Privacy Policy - in short"},"731":{"id":"/docs/legal-3","page_id":"/docs/legal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/legal#contact","content":"Contact"},"732":{"id":"/docs/legal-4","page_id":"/docs/legal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/legal"