nage Channels** inside channel tickets."],[882,"**Admin roles** are a higher tier - on channel tickets they're given **Manage Channels** inside the\nticket, and they act as the fallback when a ticket type doesn't define its own admin roles."],[726,"**Anyone curious about the settings** - the Dashboard and\nCustomization sections cover every field and button."],[680,"**Audit log**\n: A reverse-chronological record of settings, panel, blacklist and ticket changes, each with an\nactor ID and timestamp."],[321,"**Avatar** and **Banner** accept either a normal **image URL** (`https://...`) or a **data URI**\n(`data:image/png;base64,...`)."],[325,"**Avatar** and **Banner** are this server's profile images for the bot."],[326,"**Bio** is the bot's \"about me\" text in this server."],[681,"**Blacklist**\n: A list of users who cannot open tickets in a server."],[376,"**Blacklist** button"],[539,"**Blacklisted users** get an ephemeral \"You're not allowed to open tickets in this server\"\nmessage, with the reason if one was set."],[682,"**Bot profile**\n: The nickname, avatar, banner and bio the bot shows in one server, set on the server page. It does\nnot change the bot globally."],[683,"**Button panel**\n: A panel that shows one button per ticket type (max 5)."],[365,"**Buttons** - label, emoji and style for `claim`, `add`, `remove`, `rename` and `close`."],[273,"**Buttons** - one button per type. Discord allows **5** buttons per row, so the panel shows at\nmost **5** types in this mode."],[684,"**Channel ticket**\n: A private channel created for a single ticket."],[526,"**Channel tickets** are private. The bot sets permission overwrites so that:"],[685,"**Claim**\n: A staff member marking themselves as handling a ticket."],[370,"**Closing behaviour** - DM the opener a copy, delete the channel on close."],[813,"**Closing behaviour** (Customization → Closing behaviour): turn **Delete the channel on close**\noff if you want to keep the closed channel around. It is then renamed `closed-<number>`; the\ntranscript is saved either way."],[778,"**Create panel**."],[789,"**Create panel**."],[803,"**Create panel**."],[812,"**Create panel**."],[686,"**Customization**\n: The messages, colours, buttons and priorities that shape how tickets look and read. Set\nserver-wide, per panel, and per type."],[709,"**dat one ticketer** is a Discord ticketing bot. Users click a panel in your server, a private\nchannel or thread opens for them, and your staff manage it with buttons or slash commands. Every\nticket can be exported as an HTML transcript when it closes."],[304,"**Delete** - asks `Delete this panel and its message?`, removes the Discord message, and deletes\nthe panel and its types. Toast: `Panel deleted`."],[687,"**Dropdown panel**\n: A panel that shows a select menu of ticket types (max 25)."],[272,"**Dropdown** - one select menu. Up to **25** ticket types. Best when you have several options."],[303,"**Duplicate** - copies the panel and all its types, then opens the copy so you can rename it.\nToast: `Panel duplicated`."],[254,"**Edit** on a row opens `#/guild/<id>/panel/<pid>`"],[211,"**Footer**:"],[762,"**General settings**"],[793,"**General settings**"],[206,"**Header**, left to right:"],[688,"**Internal note**\n: A staff-only note on a ticket. Never shown to the opener and never included in transcripts."],[225,"**Invite the bot** in the top-right adds the bot to a new server."],[689,"**Log channel**\n: The channel that receives ticket activity and internal notes. Also used for transcripts when no\ntranscript channel is set."],[745,"**Login data** - if you sign in to the dashboard: your Discord user ID, username and avatar, held\nin a signed session cookie for the session."],[690,"**Max open tickets**\n: The per-user cap on open tickets. Staff bypass it, and a ticket type can add its own cap."],[367,"**Mention pings** - ping the opener, plus comma-separated role IDs to ping."],[594,"**never** shown to the opener or included in the transcript."],[324,"**Nickname** changes how the bot's name shows in this server only."],[692,"**Panel template**\n: A starting point in the new-panel editor - `Blank`, `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` or\n`Ban appeal`. It fills in the panel message and ticket types; everything stays editable."],[937,"**Panel templates** - `Blank`, `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user` and `Ban appeal` in the\nnew-panel editor."],[772,"**Panel**"],[781,"**Panel**"],[796,"**Panel**"],[806,"**Panel**"],[691,"**Panel**\n: A message in a channel with a dropdown or buttons that opens tickets."],[693,"**Placeholder**\n: A `{token}` in a text field that is replaced with a real value, e.g. `{username}`."],[366,"**Priorities** - add/edit/remove rows of emoji + label + id + colour."],[694,"**Priority**\n: Low / Normal / High / Urgent (or your own list). Used by the Priority button and shown on the\nwelcome embed."],[695,"**Private thread**\n: A thread only visible to its members and users with **Manage Threads**. Used for thread tickets."],[375,"**Reason (optional)** text box"],[934,"**Restyled transcripts** - the HTML transcript now uses the same\nlight/dark styling as the rest of the service, ends with the brand and site link, and shows\n`No messages.` for an empty ticket."],[932,"**Server bot profile** - the server page now has a\nBot profile (this server) card for a nickname, avatar, banner and bio\nthat apply to one server only."],[742,"**Server data** - the server ID, name and icon, and the channel/category/role IDs used in your\nconfiguration."],[724,"**Server owners & admins** who want to invite the bot and configure it - start with\nGetting started."],[936,"**Sign out link** - the dashboard header has a `Sign out` link (`/oauth/logout`)."],[885,"**Staff bypass these limits**, so they can always open a ticket to test."],[696,"**Staff**\n: Anyone with **Manage Channels**, or any role listed in Staff roles or Admin roles."],[541,"**Staff** bypass all open-ticket limits (they can always open a ticket to test)."],[725,"**Staff** who live in tickets - read Using tickets."],[935,"**Styled sign-in errors** - a failed sign-in now shows a proper page\n(`Sign-in failed` / `Sign-in error` / `Not found`) instead of plain text. See\nTroubleshooting."],[697,"**Sub-type**\n: A second choice under a ticket type, e.g. `Bug report → Crash`."],[368,"**System messages** - claimed, renamed, member added, member removed, ticket closed, transcript\nsaved."],[698,"**Tag**\n: A short free-text label staff can put on a ticket."],[703,"**Thread ticket**\n: A private thread created for a single ticket (auto-archives after 7 days; archived + locked on\nclose)."],[532,"**Thread tickets** are private threads created under the panel's thread-parent channel (or the\npanel channel). The opener is added as a member; `invitable` is off. Threads auto-archive after\n7 days (10080 minutes) of inactivity."],[743,"**Ticket data** - ticket number, opener user ID, ticket type, assigned staff, status and\ntimestamps."],[744,"**Ticket message content** - only for a ticket's own channel/thread, and only to build its\ntranscript when it closes."],[700,"**Ticket type**\n: One option on a panel, e.g. `General Support` or `Sales`."],[699,"**Ticket**\n: A single support conversation, opened from a panel and living in its own channel or thread."],[702,"**Transcript channel**\n: The channel where closed-ticket transcripts are posted. Falls back to the log channel, and the\ntranscript is always saved even if neither is set."],[466,"**Transcript channel**, if set;"],[369,"**Transcript embed** - colour, footer, title, description."],[701,"**Transcript**\n: A styled HTML copy of a ticket's messages, generated when the ticket closes."],[374,"**User ID** text box (placeholder `123456789012345678`)"],[364,"**Welcome message** - colour, title, message, footer, thumbnail URL, image URL, and a\n`Show \"Opened by\" line` checkbox."],[933,"**Wiki links everywhere** - the dashboard header and footer, the Terms, Privacy and status pages,\nand the bot's `/help` and `/about` replies now link to this wiki."],[148,"`{name}` in the **Renamed** message and `{userAvatar}` in the welcome fields are the intended\nplaceholders for those spots. `{note}` in **Ticket closed** is filled with the **Transcript\nsaved** text."],[527,"`@everyone` cannot view the channel."],[508,"`/about` - brand, author, contact details and the wiki URL, plus **Add to a server** and **Wiki**\nlink buttons."],[476,"`/blacklist`"],[497,"`/config set` keys:"],[475,"`/config`"],[507,"`/help` - a short setup guide, a pointer to the buttons inside tickets, and an **Open the wiki**\nlink button."],[477,"`/help` and `/about`"],[560,"`/panel delete` removes a panel and its types (and its message)."],[559,"`/panel list` shows every panel with its ID, channel and mode."],[558,"`/panel resend` deletes the old message (if any) and posts a new one in the panel's channel."],[473,"`/panel`"],[509,"`/panel` and `/blacklist` are staff-gated. If someone without the right role runs them they get\n`You need the **Manage Server** permission to use this command.`"],[474,"`/ticket`"],[452,"`#<number>`"],[454,"`<subject> · opener <user id> · <n> messages`"],[406,"`Blank` · `Support` · `Sales` · `Report a user` · `Ban appeal`"],[800,"`Category for new tickets`: `Sales Tickets`."],[808,"`Channel to post in`: `#appeals`."],[783,"`Channel to post in`: `#report-a-user` (or a read-only info channel)."],[798,"`Channel to post in`: `#sales`."],[774,"`Channel to post in`: `#support`."],[802,"`Default priority`: `high` for `New Order`, leave `normal` for questions."],[776,"`Panel style`: `Dropdown`."],[786,"`Panel style`: `Dropdown`."],[210,"`Sign out` goes to `/oauth/logout` and clears your dashboard session."],[785,"`Thread parent channel (thread mode)`: the channel that should hold the threads (often the panel\nchannel)."],[809,"`Ticket mode`: `Private channel` with a dedicated `Appeals` category (simpler staff access than\nprivate threads)."],[7