 settings"],[640,"2. Sign in to the dashboard"],[623,"25 with **Dropdown**, 5 with **Buttons** (Discord's row limit)."],[5,"3. Brand it (optional)"],[641,"3. Do the one-minute config"],[756,"3. Sales enquiries"],[757,"4. Ban appeals"],[6,"4. Build the panel"],[642,"4. Create your first panel"],[929,"4.0.5"],[7,"5. Smoke test"],[643,"5. Test it"],[8,"6. Before announcing"],[9,"7. First week"],[252,"A **panel** is the message users click to open a ticket. You reach the editor from the\n**Ticket panels** card on the server page:"],[279,"A **remove** button"],[256,"A `Template` dropdown with: `Blank`, `Support`, `Sales`, `Report a user`, `Ban appeal`. Picking one\nfills the fields and ticket types below with a ready-made starting point. You can still edit\neverything afterwards. The exact contents of each template are listed on\nPanel templates."],[37,"A blacklisted test user is refused (blacklist)."],[379,"A blacklisted user who clicks a panel gets an ephemeral message telling them they're not allowed,\nincluding the reason if you set one."],[455,"A button **Open** which opens the full HTML transcript in a new tab."],[462,"A footer with the brand, the export time and the service's site link."],[223,"A grid of server cards. Each shows the server icon, its name, and `Owner` or `Manager`."],[458,"A header with the ticket number, subject, and meta line: opener, message count and the brand that\nexported it."],[274,"A live mock of the panel title, description and a chip per ticket type. It updates as you type.\nUse it to sanity-check wording and colours before saving."],[715,"A message with a dropdown or buttons. Each option is a ticket type (\"Bug report\",\n\"Ban appeal\", ...). Post as many panels as you like."],[720,"A nickname, avatar, banner and bio for the bot in your server alone."],[550,"A panel is a message with a **dropdown** or **buttons**. It is posted by the dashboard (or\n`/panel create`) and edited in place whenever you save the panel. You can also re-post it with\n`/panel resend`."],[155,"A placeholder is written in curly braces, e.g. `{username}`. Anything that isn't a known token is\nshown **literally** - so if you see `{something}` in a message, it wasn't a valid token."],[180,"A reverse-chronological list of settings, panel, blacklist and ticket changes."],[931,"A running list of changes you can see in Discord or the dashboard. Everything else in the wiki\nalready describes the current behaviour."],[33,"A second click while at the cap is refused with a clear message."],[2,"A short checklist to take a server from invite to a tested, public ticket desk."],[453,"A status chip: `open`, `closed` or `deleted`"],[293,"A sub-type is a second choice under a ticket type - e.g. type `Bug report` with sub-types\n`🐛 Crash | The app closes` and `🐌 Slow | It's laggy`."],[209,"A theme button showing `light` or `dark` - it flips the whole site theme and remembers your\nchoice in the browser."],[456,"A ticket is marked `deleted` once it has been closed and its channel removed, renamed or\narchived. The transcript itself is still there - `deleted` refers to the ticket channel, not the\ntranscript."],[447,"A transcript is a self-contained HTML file of every message in a ticket, generated when the ticket\ncloses. It is saved, posted to your transcript (or log) channel, and offered as a file attachment."],[322,"A URL is fetched by the bot, must return an `image/*` content type, and must be **8 MB or\nsmaller**. Anything else is rejected with an error toast."],[519,"A user clicks a **dropdown** option or a **button** on a panel."],[883,"A user on the **blacklist** cannot open tickets at all."],[738,"Acceptable use: no harassment, spam, abuse, attempts to break or overload the service, illegal\nactivity, or reselling it as your own."],[811,"Add a **Welcome message override** asking for the case ID and the reason given."],[664,"Add at least one **Ticket type** (a label like `General Support`)."],[565,"Add User / Remove User"],[16,"Add you